ather than a more permanent sexual identity or orientation."},"skos:broader":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000404"},"skos:related":[{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001112"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001284"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001306"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002142"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002147"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002177"}],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000404"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-01-18"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-12-21"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"}},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001112","dc:identifier":"homoit0001112","skos:prefLabel":{"@language":"en","@value":"Physical affection"},"rdfs:comment":{"@language":"en","@value":"Touch between two or more people intended to arouse or convey feelings of closeness; can be used to express sexual or non-sexual intimacy and includes actions such as kissing, cuddling, embracing, and holding hands."},"skos:narrower":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000691"},"skos:related":[{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000404"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000998"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001806"}],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001112"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/physicalAffection"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-12-12"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"}},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000405","dc:identifier":"homoit0000405","skos:prefLabel":{"@language":"en","@value":"Escort services"},"rdfs:comment":{"@language":"en","@value":"Agencies that serve to connect paying clients with escorts offering services by appointment. Escort services may be less stigmatized than other forms of sex work, in part because it tends to be safer for escorts and because some escorts offer a broader range of services, including accompaniment or entertainment without the promise of sexual contact. However, the tendency to frame escorting as separate from or superior to other forms of sex work obscures the labor undertaken by escorts and perpetuates discrimination against the most marginalized and vulnerable sex workers."},"skos:broader":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001276"},"skos:related":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000406"},"skos:exactMatch":{"@id":"http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85044807"},"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000011"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/escortServices"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-06-19"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"}},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000406","dc:identifier":"homoit0000406","skos:prefLabel":{"@language":"en","@value":"Escorts"},"skos:altLabel":[{"@language":"en","@value":"Call boys"},{"@language":"en","@value":"Call girls"}],"rdfs:comment":{"@language":"en","@value":"Sex workers whose clients are required to make appointments for their services. Unlike sex workers who solicit clients on the street or in institutions like brothels, escorts typically advertise their services online, whether independently or through agencies. Escorting may be less stigmatized than other forms of sex work, in part because it tends to be safer for escorts and because some escorts offer a broader range of services, including accompaniment or entertainment without the promise of sexual contact. However, the tendency to frame escorting as separate from or superior to other forms of sex work obscures the labor undertaken by escorts and perpetuates discrimination against the most marginalized and vulnerable sex workers."},"skos:related":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000405"},"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003758"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/escorts"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-06-19"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"}},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000651","dc:identifier":"homoit0000651","skos:prefLabel":{"@language":"en","@value":"Hormones"},"rdfs:comment":{"@language":"en","@value":"Regulatory substances produced in organisms and transported throughout the body to stimulate specific cells or tissues into action. Though hormones regulate digestion, respiration, sleep, and many other bodily functions, the term is most commonly used by the general public to describe the \"sex hormones,\" or the hormones involved in puberty and sexual development, reproduction, and sexual desire."},"skos:broader":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001269"},"skos:narrower":[{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000407"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001362"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002820"}],"skos:related":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002876"},"skos:exactMatch":{"@id":"http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85061980"},"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001269"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/hormones"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2023-06-30"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"}},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000986","dc:identifier":"homoit0000986","skos:prefLabel":{"@language":"en","@value":"MtFs"},"skos:altLabel":[{"@language":"en","@value":"Males transitioning to females"},{"@language":"en","@value":"MtF transsexuals"},{"@language":"en","@value":"Male-to-female"},{"@language":"en","@value":"M2Fs"},{"@language":"en","@value":"Transsexual women"}],"rdfs:comment":{"@language":"en","@value":"MtF (male-to-female) is a mostly historical term that has been largely replaced by \"trans women.\" This is due in part to the term’s connection to the medicalisation of transgender people and its assumption that trans women are \"born\" male and become female (typically through hormones and/or surgery)."},"skos:broader":[{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000878"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001381"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001642"}],"skos:related":[{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000407"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000436"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000457"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001027"}],"skos:exactMatch":{"@id":"http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2006002132"},"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000878"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/MtFs"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-01-05"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"}},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000408","dc:identifier":"homoit0000408","skos:prefLabel":{"@language":"en","@value":"Etiology"},"rdfs:comment":{"@language":"en","@value":"Inquiries and speculations regarding the causes of sexual behaviors or diseases."},"skos:broader":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001365"},"skos:exactMatch":{"@id":"http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh00005666"},"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001365"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/etiology"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-12-13"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"}},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000409","dc:identifier":"homoit0000409","skos:prefLabel":{"@language":"en","@value":"Eurogames"},"rdfs:comment":{"@language":"en","@value":"The most important gay and lesbian sporting event in Europe, hosted by license of the European Gay and Lesbian Sport Federation (EGLSF)"},"skos:broader":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000949"},"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000861"},"dc:isReplacedBy":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000949"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/eurogames"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-08-22"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"}},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000949","dc:identifier":"homoit0000949","skos:prefLabel":{"@language":"en","@value":"LGBTQ+ sporting events"},"skos:altLabel":{"@language":"en","@value":"LGBTQ sporting events"},"rdfs:comment":{"@language":"en","@value":"Organized games or sports activities for LGBTQ+ people or communities; includes both competitive and recreational events."},"skos:broader":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000861"},"skos:related":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001929"},"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000861"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/LGBTQSportingEvents"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-12-12"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"}},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000410","dc:identifier":"homoit0000410","skos:prefLabel":{"@language":"en","@value":"Europride"},"rdfs:comment":{"@language":"en","@value":"A pan-European international event dedicated to LGBTQ+ pride that is hosted by a different European city each year"},"skos:broader":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000522"},"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003653"},"dc:isReplacedBy":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000861"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/europride"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-10-04"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"}},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000522","dc:identifier":"homoit0000522","skos:prefLabel":{"@language":"en","@value":"Gay pride"},"rdfs:comment":{"@language":"en","@value":"The recognition and celebration of gay people and culture, thereby affirming the visibility, dignity, and diversity of gay communities. This term can be used to refer to gay men specifically, but it is often used as an umbrella term for LGBTQ+ pride as a whole, particularly in historical contexts."},"skos:broader":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003653"},"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003653"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/gayPride"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-08-20"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"}},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003653","dc:identifier":"homoit0003653","skos:prefLabel":{"@language":"en","@value":"LGBTQ+ pride"},"skos:altLabel":{"@language":"en","@value":"Pride (LGBTQ)"},"rdfs:comment":{"@language":"en","@value":"The recognition and celebration of LGBTQ+ people and culture, thereby affirming the visibility, dignity, and diversity of LGBTQ+ communities."},"skos:narrower":[{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000522"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000767"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003654"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003655"}],"skos:related":[{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003246"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002386"}],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003653"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-10-22"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2025-01-26"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"}},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000411","dc:identifier":"homoit0000411","skos:prefLabel":{"@language":"en","@value":"Ex-gay movement"},"rdfs:comment":{"@language":"en","@value":"People and organizations that encourage people to resist entering or pursuing same-sex relationships, to eliminate homosexual desires, to develop heterosexual desires, and/or to enter into heterosexual relationships."},"skos:broader":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001322"},"skos:related":[{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000303"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000619"}],"skos:exactMatch":{"@id":"http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2005005425"},"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001322"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/ex-gayMovement"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-12-13"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"}},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000412","dc:identifier":"homoit0000412","skos:prefLabel":{"@language":"en","@value":"Exhibitionism"},"skos:broader":[{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000442"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001267"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001299"}],"skos:related":[{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001142"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001257"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001283"}],"skos:exactMatch":{"@id":"http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85046353"},"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000404"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/exhibitionism"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-05-15"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"}},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001257","dc:identifier":"homoit0001257","skos:prefLabel":{"@language":"en","@value":"Voyeurism"},"skos:altLabel":[{"@language":"en","@value":"Scopophilia"},{"@language":"en","@value":"Scoptophilia"}],"rdfs:comment":{"@language":"en","@value":"Practice of watching or listening to others, typically without their awareness or consent. In consensual sexual encounters, voyeurism involves watching or listening to someone undress or engage in sexual activity without actively participating."},"skos:broader":[{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000442"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001267"}],"skos:related":[{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000412"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001142"}],"skos:exactMatch":{"@id":"http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85118773"},"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000404"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/voyeurism"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-05-15"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"}},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001283","dc:identifier":"homoit0001283","skos:prefLabel":{"@language":"en","@value":"LGBTQ+ people with sexual addictions"},"skos:altLabel":{"@language":"en","@value":"LGBTQ+ people with sex addictions"},"rdfs:comment":{"@language":"en","@value":"LGBTQ+ people experiencing addiction to or dependency upon sexual activities. Only use to refer to individuals who describe themselves as having sexual addictions, not individuals whose sexual practices are perceived as promiscuous or unsafe by others."},"skos:broader":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001550"},"skos:narrower":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001539"},"skos:related":[{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000412"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000656"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001538"}],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000915"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/sexualAddiction"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-12-21"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"}},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000415","dc:identifier":"homoit0000415","skos:prefLabel":{"@language":"en","@value":"Faeries"},"skos:altLabel":[{"@language":"en","@value":"Radical Faeries"},{"@language":"en","@value":"Faes"}],"rdfs:comment":{"@language":"en","@value":"Queer people who are involved with or identify with the countercultural movement seeking to redefine queer consciousness through secular spirituality. Often but not always associated with the Radical Faeries, a loosely affiliated worldwide network that formed in the 1970s."},"skos:broader":[{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000487"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001295"}],"skos:related":[{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000948"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002230"}],"skos:closeMatch":{"@id":"http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh98004651"},"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001345"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/faeries"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-12-21"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"}},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000948","dc:identifier":"homoit0000948","skos:prefLabel":{"@language":"en","@value":"LGBTQ+ spiritual people"},"skos:altLabel":{"@language":"en","@value":"LGBTQ+ spirituality"},"rdfs:comment":{"@language":"en","@value":"LGBTQ+ people who hold spiritual beliefs or engage in spiritual practices, typically involving an understanding of something greater than human existence, whether divine or cosmic in nature."},"skos:related":[{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000415"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000928"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001218"}],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000948"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/LGBTQSpirituality"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-12-13"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"}},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002230","dc:identifier":"homoit0002230","skos:prefLabel":{"@language":"en","@value":"Fairies (Gay culture)"},"skos:altLabel":{"@language":"en","@value":"Fairy (Gay culture)"},"rdfs:comment":{"@language":"en","@value":"Pejorative term used chiefly in North America to describe gay men (or men assumed to be gay) and insult their perceived femininity. Some gay men have reclaimed this term and use it to describe themselves. Not to be confused with Faeries, the queer spiritual group."},"skos:broader":[{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000878"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001559"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001560"}],"skos:related":[{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000415"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000487"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000535"}],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000878"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-07-20"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-12-16"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"}},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000629","dc:identifier":"homoit0000629","skos:prefLabel":{"@language":"en","@value":"Heterosexual women"},"skos:altLabel":{"@language":"en","@value":"Straight women"},"rdfs:comment":{"@language":"en","@value":"Women who identify as heterosexual, or straight."},"skos:broader":[{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000627"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001509"}],"skos:narrower":[{"@id":"https://homosaurus.or