ies, gender identities, and romantic orientations that fall under the LGBTQ+ umbrella, as well as flags representing LGBTQ+ subcultures and communities."},"skos:broader":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000954"},"skos:narrower":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001232"},"skos:related":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003653"},"skos:exactMatch":{"@id":"http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2023001832"},"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000954"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-05-24"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-08-01"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"}},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003262","dc:identifier":"homoit0003262","skos:prefLabel":{"@language":"en","@value":"LGBTQ+ sex tourism"},"skos:altLabel":{"@language":"en","@value":"Sex tourism (LGBTQ)"},"rdfs:comment":{"@language":"en","@value":"The practice of traveling with the intention of soliciting sex work, typically to allow LGBTQ+ or curious people to explore sexual encounters that are illegal or stigmatized in their home countries. Sex tourism often presents ethical concerns, such as the economic gap between tourists and residents, differences in age of consent laws globally, and the selective enforcement of anti-sex work laws by police."},"skos:broader":[{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000956"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001275"}],"skos:related":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001277"},"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000956"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-05-24"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-08-01"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"}},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003279","dc:identifier":"homoit0003279","skos:prefLabel":{"@language":"en","@value":"LGBTQ+ travel guides"},"skos:altLabel":[{"@language":"en","@value":"Guide books (LGBTQ)"},{"@language":"en","@value":"LGBTQ+ guide books"},{"@language":"en","@value":"LGBTQ+ travel guide books"},{"@language":"en","@value":"Travel guide books (LGBTQ)"},{"@language":"en","@value":"Travel guides (LGBTQ)"}],"rdfs:comment":{"@language":"en","@value":"Books or other resources of information about places designed for the use of LGBTQ+ visitors or tourists, typically to direct travelers to establishments or attractions that are owned by, open to, or frequented by LGBTQ+ people. LGBTQ+ travel guides may also direct travelers to safe houses or businesses in places where LGBTQ+ people are otherwise unsafe or criminalized, as well as locations commonly used for cruising, or picking up casual sex partners."},"skos:broader":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000956"},"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000956"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-06-10"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-08-01"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"}},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001222","dc:identifier":"homoit0001222","skos:prefLabel":{"@language":"en","@value":"Queer victims of rape"},"rdfs:comment":{"@language":"en","@value":"Queer people who have experienced rape and may or may not have survived; follow the individual's preference for \"victims\" or \"survivors\" whenever possible."},"skos:broader":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000958"},"skos:narrower":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001212"},"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000915"},"dc:replaces":{"@id":"http://homosaurus.org/v2/queerVictimsOfRape"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2019-05-14"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-12-13"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"}},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001457","dc:identifier":"homoit0001457","skos:prefLabel":{"@language":"en","@value":"Transg