d from the categories of \"female\" and \"femininity\" as understood by white feminists. At the core of womanism is the idea that mainstream feminism is a movement led by white women to serve white women's goals, which can be indifferent or even oppositional to the needs of Black women. Use for resources about womanists or when an individual identifies as such."},"skos:related":[{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002272"},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003170"}],"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003176"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-01-11"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2024-02-01"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"}},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002280","dc:identifier":"homoit0002280","skos:prefLabel":{"@language":"en","@value":"Mothers of queer people"},"skos:altLabel":[{"@language":"en","@value":"Moms of queer people"},{"@language":"en","@value":"Queer people's moms"},{"@language":"en","@value":"Queer people's mothers"}],"rdfs:comment":{"@language":"en","@value":"Individuals who assume the role of mother to a queer person or queer people; use only for individuals who self-identify as mothers."},"skos:broader":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002348"},"skos:hasTopConcept":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000421"},"dc:issued":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-11-10"},"dc:modified":{"@type":"xsd:date","@value":"2022-12-16"},"@type":"skos:Concept","skos:inScheme":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3"}},{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002296","dc:identifier":"homoit0002296","skos:prefLabel":{"@language":"en","@value":"Kashmiri lesbians"},"skos:altLabel":{"@language":"en","@value":"Lesbian Kashmiris"},"rdfs:comment":{"@language":"en","@value":"Lesbians who live in or are descended from those native to the Kashmir Valley in the Indian subcontinent."},"skos:broader":{"@id":"https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002295"},"skos:h